@RULE WireWorld

Brian Silverman's WireWorld: electrons run along copper wire. A head
becomes a tail, a tail becomes wire, and wire becomes a head when one or
two of its eight neighbours are heads. Written for cellar.

@TABLE
n_states:4
neighborhood:Moore
symmetries:permute

# any state
var a={0,1,2,3}
var b=a
var c=a
var d=a
var e=a
var f=a
var g=a
var h=a
# anything but a head
var p={0,2,3}
var q=p
var r=p
var s=p
var t=p
var u=p
var v=p

# the cell first, its neighbours clockwise from north, then its next state
1,a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h,2
2,a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h,3
3,1,p,q,r,s,t,u,v,1
3,1,1,p,q,r,s,t,u,1

@COLORS
0 32 32 32
1 64 160 255
2 240 240 255
3 224 128 32
